=== sorti() Function Tests ===

1. Associative array (string keys):
   Original:  ["zebra" => "z", "apple" => "a", "banana" => "b"]
   Original unchanged:  ["zebra" => "z", "apple" => "a", "banana" => "b"]
   Sorted indices:  ["apple", "banana", "zebra"]

2. Associative array (numeric keys):
   Original:  [10 => "ten", 2 => "two", 5 => "five", 1 => "one"]
   Original unchanged:  [10 => "ten", 2 => "two", 5 => "five", 1 => "one"]
   Sorted indices:  [1, 2, 5, 10]

3. Mixed keys (numeric and string):
   Original:  ["zebra" => "z", 10 => "ten", "apple" => "a", 2 => "two"]
   Original unchanged:  ["zebra" => "z", 10 => "ten", "apple" => "a", 2 => "two"]
   Sorted indices:  [2, 10, "apple", "zebra"]

4. Source array unchanged:
   Source before:  ["zebra" => "z", "apple" => "a", "banana" => "b"]
   Source after:  ["zebra" => "z", "apple" => "a", "banana" => "b"]
   Sorted indices:  ["apple", "banana", "zebra"]

5. Access original array via sorted indices:
   Original data:  ["zebra" => 100, "apple" => 50, "banana" => 75]
   Sorted indices:  ["apple", "banana", "zebra"]
   Accessing via sorted indices:
      apple  =>  50
      banana  =>  75
      zebra  =>  100

6. Empty array:
   Original:  []
   Sorted indices:  []

7. Single element:
   Original:  ["one" => 1]
   Sorted indices:  ["one"]

8. Regular array (1-indexed):
   Original:  ["first", "second", "third"]
   Original unchanged:  ["first", "second", "third"]
   Sorted indices:  [1, 2, 3]

9. Multidimensional array (numeric indices):
   Original:  ["12" => 30, "45" => 10, "23" => 20]
   Original unchanged:  ["12" => 30, "45" => 10, "23" => 20]
   Sorted indices:  ["12", "23", "45"]
   Accessing via sorted indices:
      12  =>  30
      23  =>  20
      45  =>  10

10. Multidimensional array (string indices):
   Original:  ["row1col1" => 100, "row2col1" => 50, "row1col2" => 75]
   Original unchanged:  ["row1col1" => 100, "row2col1" => 50, "row1col2" => 75]
   Sorted indices:  ["row1col1", "row1col2", "row2col1"]
   Accessing via sorted indices:
      row1col1  =>  100
      row1col2  =>  75
      row2col1  =>  50

11. Three-dimensional array:
   Original:  ["123" => 50, "111" => 10, "222" => 30, "121" => 20]
   Original unchanged:  ["123" => 50, "111" => 10, "222" => 30, "121" => 20]
   Sorted indices:  ["111", "121", "123", "222"]

12. Multidimensional array (mixed indices):
   Original:  ["12" => "a", "xy" => "b", "23" => "c", "ab" => "d"]
   Original unchanged:  ["12" => "a", "xy" => "b", "23" => "c", "ab" => "d"]
   Sorted indices:  ["12", "23", "ab", "xy"]

=== All sorti() Tests Complete ===
